# The ground control station (gcs/) flying ArduPlane SITL on the sim's physics, as the
# operator sees it. Modelled on Mission Planner's planning docs (ardupilot.org/planner):
# where the console does something already, these say what it does; elsewhere they say what
# it should do. The console's driver (gcs/src/expect.rs, `--station --expect`) clicks the real
# console; tests that need the mission file, the terrain check, the survey grid, measuring or
# the sim's window aren't supported yet.

Section: Ground control station
  The ground station flies the plane of the sim through [[ArduPilot]]. You plan a
  [[mission]] on a map of the valley, and you write the mission to the plane. Then you arm
  the plane, and you throw it. The ground station talks to ArduPlane with [[MAVLink]], as
  Mission Planner and QGroundControl do.

  The console is one window with a set of screens. The [[tactical map]] (TACTICAL SITUATION)
  is in the middle. Its buttons are along the top: FOLLOW, GOTO, PLAN, ALT-, the plan
  altitude, ALT+, +TKOF, +RTL, CLEAR, UPLOAD, DOWNLOAD, EDIT and WP1. The vehicle command
  screen has ARM, DISARM and a button for each flight mode. Start with
  [[From plan to flight]].

Vocabulary:
  State: the link is connected | lost
  State: the vehicle is disarmed | armed
    Shows: armed: the ARMED annunciator lights up
    Shows: disarmed: the ARMED annunciator goes out
  State: the autopilot mode is MANUAL | FBWA | FBWB | CRUISE | AUTO | RTL | LOITER | CIRCLE | GUIDED | TAKEOFF
    Set: press {value} on the vehicle command screen
    Shows: the {value} button lights up
    Shows: stays the same: the mode does not change, and the AUTO button shows AUTO: NO MISSION?
  State: the map tool is pan | PLAN | GOTO
    Shows: pan: the map is back to panning
    Shows: PLAN: the PLAN button lights up
    Shows: GOTO: the GOTO button lights up
  State: the plan has 0..650 items
    Shows: the UPLOAD button reads UPLOAD {value}
    Shows: goes up by 1: a new marker appears at the end of the dashed plan, and the count on UPLOAD goes up by 1
    Shows: goes down by 1: the last marker goes away from the dashed plan, and the count on UPLOAD goes down by 1
    Shows: stays the same: the dashed plan and the count on UPLOAD do not change
  State: the plan altitude is 10..300 m
    Set: set the plan altitude to {value} with ALT- and ALT+
    Shows: the plan altitude between ALT- and ALT+ reads {value} m
    Shows: goes up by 10 m: the plan altitude between ALT- and ALT+ goes up by 10 m
    Shows: goes down by 10 m: the plan altitude between ALT- and ALT+ goes down by 10 m
    Shows: stays the same: the plan altitude between ALT- and ALT+ does not change
  State: the last plan item is none | TAKEOFF | WAYPOINT | LOITER_UNLIM | LOITER_TURNS | LAND | RTL
    Set: change the last item's command to {value}
    Shows: the last item of the dashed plan is {value}
  State: the takeoff is planned | not planned
    Shows: planned: the first item of the plan is a takeoff at home
    Shows: not planned: the plan has no takeoff
  State: the newest waypoint is at the plan altitude | at another altitude
    Shows: at the plan altitude: the new waypoint goes at the altitude between ALT- and ALT+
    Shows: at another altitude: the waypoints that are already in the plan keep their altitude
  State: the vehicle mission is empty | up to date | out of date
    Shows: up to date: the solid line of the mission on the vehicle is the same as the dashed plan
    Shows: out of date: the dashed plan and the solid line of the mission on the vehicle are different
    Shows: stays the same: the solid line of the mission on the vehicle does not change
  State: the home position is set | not set
    Shows: set: the map marks home where the plane was armed
  State: the waypoints are unchecked | clear of the terrain | too low somewhere
    Shows: clear of the terrain: each waypoint is above the ground below it
  State: the mission file is missing | up to date | out of date
    Shows: up to date: the file has the plan as it is now
    Shows: out of date: the plan is different from the file
  State: the measured distance is hidden | shown
    Shows: shown: the distance between the two points is shown on the map
  State: the vehicle's current item is 0..650
    Shows: item {value} is the current item, which is magenta on the map
    Shows: goes up by 1: the next item becomes the current item, which is magenta on the map
    Shows: stays the same: the current item does not change

  Event: the operator toggles the planning tool
    Say: press PLAN
  Event: the operator toggles the fly-to tool
    Say: press GOTO
  Event: the operator clicks the map
    Say: click the map
  Event: the operator right-clicks the map
    Say: right-click the map
  Event: the operator raises the plan altitude
    Say: press ALT+
  Event: the operator lowers the plan altitude
    Say: press ALT-
  Event: the operator adds a takeoff
    Say: press +TKOF
  Event: the operator adds a return home
    Say: press +RTL
  Event: the operator clears the plan
    Say: press CLEAR
  Event: the operator uploads the plan
    Say: press UPLOAD
  Event: the operator downloads the vehicle's mission
    Say: press DOWNLOAD
  Event: the operator edits the vehicle's mission
    Say: press EDIT
  Event: the operator restarts the mission
    Say: press WP1
  Event: the operator arms the vehicle
    Say: press ARM. Then press CONFIRM ARM in three seconds or less
  Event: the operator disarms the vehicle
    Say: press DISARM
  Event: the operator switches to AUTO
    Say: press AUTO
  Event: the operator switches to AUTO anyway
    Say: press AUTO. The button shows AUTO: NO MISSION? for four seconds. In that time, press it again
  Event: the operator saves the plan to a file
  Event: the operator loads the plan from the file
  Event: the operator checks the heights against the terrain
  Event: the operator draws a survey grid
  Event: the operator measures between two points
  Event: the pilot throws the plane in the sim
    Say: click the sim window. Then press Space to throw the plane
  Event: the plane reaches a waypoint
  Event: the plane reaches the last item

  Phrase: the console is connected to a plane on the ground
    Say: install Rust and Docker Desktop. Then run `cd gcs && cargo run --release -- --station`. The first time, it builds ArduPlane [[SITL]], which takes approximately 15 minutes. After that, it starts in a few seconds. Three windows open: the console, the [[sensor feed]] and the sim. The console connects to the plane. The plane is on the ground and disarmed, in MANUAL, with home set and no plan. Wait until the ARM button shows ARM, not ARM: NOT READY
    Given the link is connected
    And the vehicle is disarmed
    And the autopilot mode is MANUAL
    And the map tool is pan
    And the plan has 0 items
    And the plan altitude is 40 m
    And the last plan item is none
    And the takeoff is not planned
    And the vehicle mission is empty
    And the home position is set
    And the waypoints are unchecked
    And the mission file is missing
    And the measured distance is hidden
    And the plane is on the ground
    And the vehicle's current item is 0

  Phrase: the operator plans two waypoints
    Say: click the map at two points over the valley floor near home
    When the operator clicks the map
    When the operator clicks the map

  Phrase: the operator plans three waypoints
    Say: click the map at three points over the valley floor near home
    When the operator clicks the map
    When the operator clicks the map
    When the operator clicks the map

Background:
  Given the console is connected to a plane on the ground
